":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'tu' with one installed app matching: the divider between direct children (setup) and deeper entries (install.tui) is no longer drawn"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Base, root `tu`: `setup | install.tui ... apps.code ...`. Head: `apps.code | setup install.tui ...`. The current-menu rows and deeper rows now share one section. The PR says only \"with the divider following them\". Our TKDP rewrite (\"one divider separates the apps from all menu entries\") and witness (menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1404) codify the new form. That is our reading, not the author's statement.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":709},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1404},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: is dropping the direct/deeper divider whenever an app matches intended?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'e' with 200 installed apps: index of the first menu row in the result list"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Every matching app now precedes every menu row. The manual differential measured the first menu row at index 20 with 20 apps, 56 with 63 and 179 with 200 for a one-letter query (base: index 0). The PR screenshots show one-app cases only.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: with many installed apps, do short queries bury every menu entry?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Burial at scale\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:searchScore"],"scenario":"property: for every tier value and kind, max app score*1000+depth*25+order < min menu/link score*1000"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The invariant \"exceeds every match tier\" lives only in a comment. A future tier at 98 or above would silently let a menu row outrank an app. The MC/DC replay pins today's values, but not the invariant itself.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: does the -100 bias stay above every tier if a tier >= 98 is added? (opinion: name the constant)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Tier-gap invariant property test\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"These requirements are verified by test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh and menu-acceptance-test.sh, which need a live Hyprland/Quickshell session and are not in any audit suite. Their outcomes are unobserved at this revision, so these requirements are not tested here. The gap predates the PR and reaches them only through the file-level Menu.qml trace. The disclosures still prevent readiness.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-8CQ4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-NM45","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"10 test_outcome_unobserved disclosures: live compositor/acceptance tests are in no audit suite (baseline gap)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent for this JS/QML change, so the empty spec-gap list proves nothing about uncodified connections (review.scope approximations). Callers of searchScore: only Menu.qml searchScore() to rebuildDisplay, plus test assertions; resolveRoute does not use it. This comes from reading the code, not from engine-verified facts.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable); uncodified connections cannot be detected","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:64857d31a23a01153267f5d5704d5683fc633eedaa2ef42388487ea55079c377","packageIdentity":"epkg-0795462b1ac30cc2d1cd48a6d20b6e76085704e1b6d50b2cc8b7b0c1b27cfb65","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"The change deliberately reorders every menu search, and Enter's target changes for many queries (including exact-label menu entries). It carries 4 unapproved compatibility changes. The configured differential does not exercise ranking, and 10 requirements in file-level scope have unobserved live-test outcomes. The engine risk is low on gates and coverage. This is advisory only."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":8,"rationale":"Pins the maintainer's decision either way: root 'system' with btop installed, and 'terminal' with Alacritty. Assert which row is first.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1355}],"title":"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app"},{"forClaim":9,"rationale":"Assert the boundary count and position for root 'tu' with one matching app. This turns D5 into a decided, pinned behaviour.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1404}],"title":"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present"},{"forClaim":10,"rationale":"With 200 synthetic app rows, record the index of the first menu row for one-letter queries, plus a bound the maintainer accepts.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"title":"Burial at scale"},{"forClaim":11,"rationale":"Enumerate tiers x kinds x realistic depth/order and assert app max < menu min. Fails loudly if a tier >= 98 is added.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377}],"title":"Tier-gap invariant property test"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #12223 (ax1g) makes installed apps rank above menu entries in menu search. Two code changes: `searchScore` app bias goes from -5 to -100 (MenuModel.js:377), which exceeds the whole tier range (tiers 0-80), so any matching app outranks any matching menu entry; and `rebuildDisplay` pins matching app rows above the current menu's own rows and sets the divider after them (Menu.qml:695-713). Later mirror commits are our proof work, not upstream: SJ7P/TKDP rewritten to the PR's intent, rebuildDisplay witnesses, the #10340 test in reporter-expectation mode, citation re-points, REVIEW-261001-EAD8/-ER1B, a KI note, a trace re-review.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** The changed decisions are measured and covered (2/2, 0 uncovered lines/outcomes). SJ7P and TKDP show observed passing tests; 54/54 ingested tests passed. I re-ran both node suites (pass) and ran base vs head `rebuildDisplay`: `vsc` puts VS Code first, `system` puts btop above the exact-label System menu, and at root `tu` the direct/deeper divider moves to below the app.\n\n**Compatibility.** The package lists 4 unapproved compat changes (compat_change_unapproved, prevents ready): the replay MC/DC expected values (-5000/5000 to -100000/-90000), the #10340 test rewrite, and 2 removed-behaviour items in its helper. All four follow the PR's stated intent; none is approved, only a human reviewer can do that. The configured differential ran 213 inputs with no difference, but its harness covers JSONC parsing and the menu request lifecycle, not search ranking. It is no evidence about ranking.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Should a keyword-only app match beat an exact-label menu entry (`system` to btop, `terminal`)? (2) Is losing the direct/deeper divider when any app matches intended? Our TKDP rewrite codifies it but the PR text only says the divider follows the apps. (3) With many apps, short queries bury menu entries.\n\n**Traceability.** 2 requirements modified (SJ7P, TKDP), 39 code_changed via the file-level Menu.qml trace. No spec-gap candidates, but change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable), so no uncodified connection could be detected.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** 10 test_outcome_unobserved disclosures come from live Hyprland/Quickshell tests (menu-compositor-test.sh, menu-acceptance-test.sh) that are in no audit suite. Those requirements are not tested here. Readiness is not_assessed; next decision human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved)."}
